{"title":"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1a\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1a</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1b\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1b</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the least positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11da9703923a6cb51f62c3afafa1397a376a4ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> is a product of at least four not necessarily distinct primes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693812359c092bdf5b82d8919499a4efa74639b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(m-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> is the product of two consecutive integers, so it is always even. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0c03cfffc07282e9240ec1cd6bd5c5905ba169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(m-1)+11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> is odd and never divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus any prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d50bf6ffa9ffe5a8f836ce2eea927912454ccd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-m+11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/1/0715d8733fc0be54f2fb817db79b7aa5839ccce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4m^2-4m+44=(2m-1)^2+43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"262\" height=\"19\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69657d6b8ba092e214640c83412a7b27d191aec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2m-1)^2\\equiv -43\\pmod{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" />. We can verify that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c0ab5e501a1ba82a8350def08ddc9aed55d2ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-43$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" /> is not a perfect square mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> for each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/1694fae42fa43a56bd16255ab21f4c3f7b5c2b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3,5,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, all prime factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d50bf6ffa9ffe5a8f836ce2eea927912454ccd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-m+11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d76f2acb1604c82eae3534c32d7a03837eb34c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8a0634f39cbeb1df3d8ab97c64b5e777c0e6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11 = pqrs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" /> for primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79cfff636995381725b693609db1fe8e23eebae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11\\le p \\le q \\le r \\le s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />. From here, we could go a few different ways:\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1a\">Solution 1a</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1a\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb5a1402e5a2040d6bf90ffcbcdf8a62633c8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />; then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/5537eb35b5b6effd965537b3a18164831d851ea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-m+11=11qrs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. Reducing modulo 11, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc0ce12693738a52dfc85c7f1cd40afc74e7c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\equiv  1,0 \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a517a0df90b08616046069b79b6c1e99b1c1e785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(11k\\pm 1)+1 = qrs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/0478253db7616230055e417361da4eead915a381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />. Then we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31eecb710fa125938957876b84f4cd49c7ee4bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11k^2\\pm k + 1 = 11rs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />, which leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4277f7df2a0c5be3015f82373b63657e97426f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\equiv \\pm 1 \\pmod{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" />, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/92702111d15d72444dba28e8810518a6f1ebedac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in \\{1,10,12,21,23,\\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f037b42832035290b739549c564e6e1b7ab515cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> (impossible)! Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afd9b066c6c1fb6ef4383cb93bbabe6521c36d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c83b4dd2365f676e00f208d53f8de1032dd9400a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs=101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, a prime (impossible). Finally, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a53386cd894f9012b606b6a52e7377fd13869a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6ae0b667d9e4cd5235f0f5046e7c4fd2be6f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs=143=11\\cdot 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d53ac70dd7ceae2e5fc2110b45cc338128365258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=11k= \\boxed{132}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"133\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1b\">Solution 1b</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1b\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8a0634f39cbeb1df3d8ab97c64b5e777c0e6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11 = pqrs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" /> for primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183e357da43d7aa3f52056961a3ab526f6bc0159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r, s\\ge11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/57799badc364774a511ff48409fdebe2fb416412.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r, s = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/9243f79b0cd9c1b612364269e1d7239730c7d702.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-m+11=11^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />. We can multiply this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and complete the square to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/226e8781acb2e0f9759c5ce757b8f33084c40db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2m-1)^2=4\\cdot 11^4-43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"19\" />. But \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9b90d2b2c0557d4d6fb3924ab0c0d7557889937.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2\\cdot 11^2-1)^2=4\\cdot 11^4-4\\cdot 11^2+1 &lt;4\\cdot 11^4-43&lt;(2\\cdot 11^2)^2,\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"19\" />\nhence we have pinned a perfect square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/226e8781acb2e0f9759c5ce757b8f33084c40db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2m-1)^2=4\\cdot 11^4-43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"19\" /> strictly between two consecutive perfect squares, a contradiction. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5df739c152cb61fdbc614df6834609425039223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqrs \\ge 11^3 \\cdot 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/9/f696dbbe1a73ab2c9ae971475e699d1f05245aa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-m+11\\ge 11^3\\cdot 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0625a83f142cb8cf8004e2b22fc4ed4681753f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-132)(m+131)\\ge0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" />. From the inequality, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/13431358361e518dd8e18d3a7d86e2f1a303827a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\ge 132$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef55af6ad375c9f79a07b4ffe05245358526cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132^2 - 132 + 11 = 11^3 \\cdot 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/14305523a19cfc9da863393a14f0768bf5a4e9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\boxed{132}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"23\" /> and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be30bf51cc05760692c7ef6afeb031912331acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3,5,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972e1408668c0294b9c65b022f60a690b43ed2e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\not |$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"12\" height=\"20\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11da9703923a6cb51f62c3afafa1397a376a4ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />. This can be done by just testing all residue classes. \n</p><p>For example, we can test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4e9aee52bb396ab837d7736ab7c73db8f67357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\equiv 0 \\mod 2$\" width=\"111\" height=\"12\" />  or  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d7f3ff1d1878cf47a47dd1db543c3d96fba664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\equiv 1 \\mod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" />  to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11da9703923a6cb51f62c3afafa1397a376a4ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> is not divisible by 2.\n</p><p>Case 1: m = 2k  \n</p>\n<pre>      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd0e67177ca755e7ea549fe85f29eb5c9058bbd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11  \\equiv 2(2 \\cdot k^2 - k + 5) +1 \\equiv 1 \\mod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"379\" height=\"19\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Case 2: m = 2k+1  \n</p>\n<pre>      <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a5191e1d8a4accb76726c2571f98915e8147d0e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11  \\equiv 2(2 \\cdot k^2 + k + 5) +1 \\equiv 1 \\mod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"381\" height=\"21\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Now, we can test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d684584a9269d53207fbc5df43692e0bee332770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11 = 11^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />, which fails, so we test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07eaf48f57c2a6f8cb1261c8c0aec43cd35aa66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - m + 11 = 11^3 \\cdot 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />, and we get m = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/17531b756bc19a5c07c7f1ab8ce1cddf4bb4097c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>-AlexLikeMath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KRleD8iDRhI\">https://youtu.be/KRleD8iDRhI</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I\" title=\"2016 AIME I\">2016 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2016\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 1